00:36:53,793 --> 00:36:59,793
Whiplash is a 2014 American independent psychological drama film written and
directed by Damien Chazelle, and starring Miles Teller, J.

11
00:40:35,172 --> 00:40:41,172
Simmons, and Paul Reiser.

12
00:44:16,551 --> 00:44:22,551
It focuses on an ambitious music student and aspiring jazz drummer (Teller),
who is pushed to his limit by his abusive instructor (Simmons).

13
00:47:57,931 --> 00:48:03,931
The film was produced by Bold Films, Blumhouse
Productions, and Right of Way Films.

14
00:51:39,310 --> 00:51:45,310
Sony Pictures acquired distribution rights for most of the world, releasing the film under Sony Pictures Classics in North America, Germany, and Australia, and
Stage 6 Films in the UK, Scandinavia, Benelux, Eastern Europe (excluding the CIS), Greece, South Africa, Spain, Italy, Portugal and Latin America.

15
00:55:20,689 --> 00:55:26,689
Chazelle completed the script in 2013, drawing upon his experiences
in a "very competitive" jazz band in high school.

16
00:59:02,068 --> 00:59:08,068
Soon after, Right of Way and Blumhouse helped Chazelle turn fifteen
pages of the screenplay into an 18-minute short film.

17
01:02:43,448 --> 01:02:49,448
The short film received acclaim after debuting at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival,
which attracted investors to produce the complete version of the script.

18
01:06:24,827 --> 01:06:30,827
Filming took place in September 2013 throughout Los Angeles over twenty days.

19
01:10:06,206 --> 01:10:12,206
The film explores concepts of perfectionism, dedication, and
success, and deconstructs the concept of ambition.

20
01:13:47,586 --> 01:13:53,586
Whiplash premiered in competition at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival on January 16, as the festival's
opening film, where it won the Audience Award Dramatic and the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic.

21
01:17:28,965 --> 01:17:34,965
The film opened in limited release domestically in the United States and Canada on October 10,
2014, gradually expanding to over 500 screens and finally closing on March 26, 2015.

22
01:21:10,344 --> 01:21:16,344
The film received acclaim for its screenplay, direction,
editing, sound mixing, and performances.

23
01:24:51,724 --> 01:24:57,724
It grossed $50 million on a $3.3 million budget
during its original theatrical run.

24
01:28:33,103 --> 01:28:39,103
The film received multiple accolades, winning Academy Awards for Best Film Editing and Best
Sound Mixing, and was nominated for Best Picture and Best Adapted Screenplay.

25
01:32:14,482 --> 01:32:20,482
Simmons's performance won the Academy, Golden Globe, BAFTA, Critics' Choice,
and Screen Actors Guild awards for Best Supporting Actor.

26
01:35:55,862 --> 01:36:01,862
It has since been assessed as one of the best films of the
2010s, the 21st century, and of all time.

27
01:39:37,241 --> 01:39:43,241
The film explores themes of new york city, jazz,
musician, obsession, music teacher.

28
01:43:18,620 --> 01:43:24,620
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
